---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ISSUES_URL, REPO_URL } from '../lib/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy policy — Sticky Reminder"
  description="How Sticky Reminder handles reminder data locally, which browser permissions it uses, and how to delete your data."
>
  <article class="container legal-page">
    <header class="legal-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Your reminders stay on your device</h1>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Sticky Reminder does not collect, sell, share or transmit personal data. It has no account,
        analytics, advertising, remote API or backend service.
      </p>
      <p class="legal-date">Effective and last updated: August 18, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Data the extension handles</h2>
      <p>When you create a reminder, the extension handles the information you enter:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>reminder title</li>
        <li>optional reminder note</li>
        <li>scheduled date and time</li>
        <li>repeat setting and completion state</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information is stored only in the browser's local extension storage on your device. It
        is used only to display, schedule and notify you about your reminders. Sticky Reminder does
        not send it to the developer or third parties, and does not use it for advertising,
        profiling or credit decisions.
      </p>
      <p>
        The extension does not read your browsing history, page content, location, contacts or
        activity on other websites. It does not request host permissions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <dl class="legal-permissions">
        <div>
          <dt><code>alarms</code></dt>
          <dd>Schedules a reminder for its due time.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt><code>notifications</code></dt>
          <dd>Displays the reminder through the browser's native notification system.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt><code>storage</code></dt>
          <dd>Saves reminders in local extension storage on your device.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Reminder data stays in local extension storage until you delete the reminder, clear the
        extension's data or uninstall the extension. The developer cannot access or recover this
        data because it is never received by a developer-run service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Browser backup, enterprise-management or device-sync features outside Sticky Reminder's
        control may handle local browser data according to the browser or device provider's own
        policies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Local backup files</h2>
      <p>
        The options page can export reminders to a JSON file and import that file later. Both
        actions are initiated by you. Export uses the browser's normal download mechanism, import
        reads only the file you select, and Sticky Reminder does not upload either the file or its
        contents.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Sticky Reminder does not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including
        children, because it does not transmit or receive user data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        Material changes will be published here and in the source repository with a new “Last
        updated” date. A change requiring new permissions or data handling will also be disclosed in
        the relevant store listing and release notes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions, <a href={`${ISSUES_URL}/new?labels=privacy&title=Privacy%20question`}>
          open a privacy issue</a
        > without including sensitive reminder content. Security vulnerabilities should use the
        repository's <a href={`${REPO_URL}/security/advisories/new`}>private advisory form</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
